{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Follow-up to the MCP cross-session warning story (734d). That story covers all single-ticket MUTATION tools plus show_ticket, including transition_ticket/reopen_ticket (via an additive dict key). Three single-ticket tools remain deferred because they return a contract the additive approach cannot ride without a breaking or disproportionate change: check_ac and quality_check return GateResultOut (READ_ONLY gate-verdict tools sharing one model, not the mutation the feature targets), and declare_no_file_impact returns a bare 'ok' str whose outputSchema would have to change type. Extend the cross-session warning to these three (a new optional field on GateResultOut for check_ac/quality_check; a return-shape change for declare_no_file_impact). The CLI surface already warns on the corresponding verbs, so this closes the remaining MCP structured-response parity gap."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787890447643801001,"uuid":"2bf42776-b238-4812-8b0a-78b2583ab30a"}